# bashqueues file key provider example
# Contract release: 0.18.15
#
# This provider is intentionally local, boring, and inspectable.
# Enterprise installs can replace it later with PKI, Vault/HSM,
# IBM HPCS, Azure Key Vault, Microsoft, LDAP-backed trust, or another
# normalized provider. Providers return data only; never shell.

QUEUEBASH_KEY_PROVIDER=file
QUEUEBASH_FILE_KEY_REGISTRY=/etc/queuebash/policy/keys/key_registry.tsv
QUEUEBASH_FILE_KEY_DEFAULT=deny
